SUMMARY:(Overnight) Craggy Pinnacle\, Catawba Falls and More!
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Hiking and Outdoors Group\nIn this western NC Hallowe
 en weekend camping trip\, we'll explore the Blue Ridge Parkway and hike Cr
 aggy Pinnacle including Craggy Gardens then go to the Visitor Center. We'l
 l also hike to Catawba Falls waterfall and car camp at Curtis Creek Campgr
 ound. On Sunday\, on our way home\, we'll hike the Linville Falls waterfal
 l trail at Linville Gorge to see the fall colors there as well. I'll have 
 Halloween candy to share on this trip.\n\n**Important Information before y
 ou RSVP:**\n-I've booked an extra campsite that can fit up to two 2-person
  tents. The first two people to RSVP can use that campsite. Campsite rate 
 is $18. Once you RSVP\, I'll let you know if you are one of the two camper
 s that can use the extra campsite\n-Go to Recreation.gov to book any addit
 ional campsites at Curtis Creek Campground.\n-The first two campsites are 
 close to each other so we can carpool if needed\n-Please respond to any me
 ssages I send to you. Failure to respond will result in your RSVP being re
 moved. A history of no-shows or late cancellations may affect your RSVP\n\
 nWe'll meet in the Chapel Hill area. I'll post the meeting by Wednesday ni
 ght. Please share the cost of gas with your drivers.\n\nDon't forget to br
 ing your camping equipment\, food\, water and snacks\, daypack and clothin
 g layers (jacket\, gloves\, hat).\nOur first destination will be Craggy Pi
 nnacle which is about 4hrs away. From there we will continue our adventure
  then check-in at the campground by 5PM to set-up and hang out and eat din
 ner at the campground. I'll leave open the option to have dinner in Black 
 Mountain or Asheville. Sunday morning we'll pack up our campsite\, drive t
 o Linville Falls\, then head home.\n\nBy participating in this event\, you
  agree to the terms below:\nTRIP PARTICIPANT WAIVER OF LIABILITY I fully r
 ealize that this activity involves a risk of personal injury\, property da
 mage\, or loss of my person or property. I hereby for myself\, my heirs\, 
 executors and administrators\, and same for persons with whom are in my pa
 rty\, waive and release any claims or rights against Triangle Hiking & Out
 doors Group (THOG)\, all of its owners and coordinators for any and all in
 jury\, damages or loss to my person or property incurred during this activ
 ity. I also understand that THOG organizers are not required\, nor should 
 it be assumed that they are CPR/First Aid/Wilderness Survival Certified an
 d I am responsible for my own personal safety.\n\nQuestions or comments ab
 out this event?\nPlease comment below or message me on Meetup.\n-Larredo
