SUMMARY:Fall Foliage 2027: Lake Placid\, NY & The Adirondacks
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Hiking and Outdoors Group\nJoin THOG for another epic
  trip to Lake Placid\, NY and the Adirondack Mountains. Instead of a solar
  eclipse\, the main event will be the spectacular Fall Colors in northern 
 New York. Other highlights of this trip include the Fall activities in and
  near Lake Placid\, Whiteface Mountain and the surrounding region as well 
 the hikes on the summit trails in The Adirondacks.\n\nPLEASE read this eve
 nt description carefully\n\nOur overnight accommodations in Lake Placid wi
 ll be at one of the newest hotels. Note: Hotel availability is limited due
  to the popularity of this area in the fall.\n\nThis will be another two-d
 ay road trip event with a hotel stay at around the half-way mark. There wi
 ll be an option to fly in as well.\n\n**RSVP’s are now open! RSVP Instru
 ctions below!**\nTrip will be from September 22\, 2027- September 28\, 202
 7\nHotel stay in Allentown\, PA on the night of 09/22/27 and 09/27/27\nLak
 e Placid stay will be (4 Nights) from 09/23/27-09/26/27 (Thursday-Monday m
 orning)\n-Add yourself to the waiting list\n-You will be sent the hotel in
 formation for Lake Placid\, NY and Allentown\, PA through Meetup Messages\
 n-Make your reservations or contact and team up with someone on the waitin
 g list to share a room with first to reduce costs then reserve room\n-Once
  your reservations are confirmed\, you will be added to the "Going" list\n
 -Each THOG member will be allowed one guest as their plus one.\n\nOur trip
  begins on Wednesday\, September 22\, 2027 from the Triangle with an overn
 ight stop in Allentown\, PA. On day two\, we will stop at a waterfall alon
 g the way\, as we make our way to Lake Placid. We’ll then spend four ama
 zing days in the Lake Placid/Adirondack Mtn region. We depart Lake Placid 
 on September 27 to head to Allentown. The next morning we leave and arrive
  in the Triangle that evening. Our drive up and down the US will include s
 trategic stops along the way to make the road trip enjoyable.\nOur itinera
 ry will include:\n\\- Summit hikes and other hikes in the Adirondacks to d
 o some leaf peeping which may include Whiteface Mountain\\\, Owl Head Over
 look\\\, Coney Mountain\\\, OK Slip Falls\\\, High Falls Gorge\\\, Azure M
 ountain\\\, and others\\. In addition\\\, we’ll visit some waterfalls\\.
 \n\\- Oktoberfest celebration on Whiteface Mountain as well as hike to the
  Whiteface Mountain summit which has amazing views at over 4\\\,800ft\\.\n
 \\- Great Adirondack Moose Festival at Indian Lake\\\, NY if it's that wee
 kend\\\,\n-Exploring Lake Placid Fall events and downtown\n-Visiting Olymp
 ic Village\, the Olympic Museum and ice skating in Olympic Center.\nWe wil
 l have a more detailed itinerary as the trip gets closer. Please stay toge
 ther as a group during this event. If you are wanting to do other things s
 eparate from the group\, this trip may not be for you.\n\nTRAVEL COSTS ass
 ociated with this event include hotel for a total of 6 nights and gas shar
 ing costs\, which are estimated to be around $1\,300 but can be reduced if
  you share hotel rooms. This doesn’t include the costs of food and drink
 s\, admission to the venues\, or souvenirs.\n\nOnce we know how many peopl
 e will be going on this trip\, we'll form carpools. We will need enough dr
 ivers for the trip up to Lake Placid and back. I'll be planning this trip 
 in such a way that it will be as comfortable\, accommodating and fun as po
 ssible.\nIf you decide to fly\, let me know first before making your reser
 vation.\n\nIMPORTANT: We will have an in-person meeting for those going on
  this trip. It will take place sometime in March 2027 to discuss some trip
  logistics and updates to the itinerary. Please plan to attend.\n\nBy part
 icipating in this event\, you agree to the terms below:\n\nTRIP PARTICIPAN
 T WAIVER OF LIABILITY I fully realize that this activity involves a risk o
 f personal injury\, property damage\, or loss of my person or property. I 
 hereby for myself\, my heirs\, executors and administrators\, and same for
  persons with whom are in my party\, waive and release any claims or right
 s against Triangle Hiking & Outdoors Group (THOG)\, all of its owners and 
 coordinators for any and all injury\, damages or loss to my person or prop
 erty incurred during this activity. I also understand that THOG organizers
  are not required\, nor should it be assumed that they are CPR/First Aid/W
 ilderness Survival Certified and I am responsible for my own personal safe
 ty.\nQuestions about this event?\nPlease comment below or send me a Meetup
  message.\n-Larredo
